  "implemented": [
    "Opt-in nonvirtual dxfRW::setDxfTablesWriteInspector observes the exact existing staged/backpatched TABLES body/profile before append, with the same expiring view and mutation contract as OBJECTS inspection.",
    "One shared inspection helper preserves empty-callback behavior, RAII guard restoration and per-attempt atomic rollback. No new DRW_Interface virtual callback or section-sized copy/decoding pass for empty inspectors.",
    "Internal bounded scanner streams selected APPID/LAYER name/identity/scope candidates using production ASCII/Binary value readers. TABLE framing, primary handle/name/flags/versioned owner and exact ordered subclass presence are checked independently of metadata and tolerant model defaults.",
    "Balanced102 groups cannot spoof primary name/handle/owner; repeated selected tables and malformed/unclosed framing invalidate the whole scan, including previous callbacks. No section-sized row/model inventory is retained.",
    "Per-name decode-event counters detect repeated identical issues without contaminating a later clean row. Unknown legacy profiles stay unqualified even for ASCII; modern UTF8 ignores irrelevant legacy metadata.",
    "Ignored nested read/write/readAscii calls during TABLES or OBJECTS inspection now fail the outer attempt without admitting a nested scope. Ordinary callbacks and consumer finalizer keep their existing non-mutating whole-operation rejection.",
    "Dedicated small symbol-output test target avoids legacy private-keyword test macros. Existing whole-operation-admission and consumer-finalizer suites gain fast focused selectors."
  ],
